Highlights:

On dlvl3 or so I found a wand of wishing which helped a lot. I got the 
Orb of Fate (without guilt!), gray dragon scale mail, scrolls of 
genocide, and gauntlets of power. This left me with one or two wishes 
I wanted to save. Sokoban gave a bag of holding, which was just as 
well because I decided early on that I would like the shield for 
reflection and the amulet for lifesaving.

I found two magic markers from a bones file in the mines that I used 
for getting rid of all the monsters I can't stand (L, h), and others 
that are annoying (; and R) and nurse dancing in Sokoban.

My character played during the full moon and got hit by a werewolf. I 
lost a t-shirt and my only source of magic resistance from that. At 
some point I got an amulet of lifesaving, but I did not want to chance 
Tiamat with repeatedly using disintegration breath on me. I used my 
last wish to get a reflection shield to fight Tiamat and killed her to 
get the Sceptre of Might (which gives magic resistance). The quest was 
a bit odd. Why exactly would Tiamat want some odd Sceptre that a tribe 
of neanderthals value? It's a piece of junk when you find it too. Not 
even corrosion proof and no enchantments.

I polypiled a lot of stuff to try for some form of levitation, a 
t-shirt, or cloaks. In the end I got some useful rings (polymorph, 
polymorph control, free action, teleport control) but no levitation, 
no t-shirt, and no cloaks. I found a polymorph trap a level or two 
before Medusa and did the cockatrice-egg-laying thing there. After 
laying egg a few eggs, a white dragon came around a corner and almost 
one shotted me :O Luckily it killed itself from stoning.

By the time I got to Medusa I STILL had not gotten some form of 
levitation. I used scrolls of earth and wands of cold to get across. 
Luckily the statue had some levitation boots. The castle was really 
easy but the dragons did not give any scales and the armor was 
useless. I went back a bit and fully cleared levels out until I killed 
a black dragon that did drop scales, which I used for my armor. I used 
a wish on a cloak of magic resistance for magic cancellation and a 
form of backup magic resistance. I saved the rest of the wishes and 
buffed up my armor/weapons.

Gehennom was not as bad as I thought it would be, but it was WAY 
longer than what I expected! Asmodeus got killed via a rubber chicken 
that was wandering around next to him. Baalzebub accepted my bribe of 
60 some zorkmids, laughed at me, and left. (perhaps there should be a 
floor value to the bribe check.. 60 is rediculously low to accept).

The Orcus fight was pretty short. After throwing 2 cockatrice eggs and 
missing I decided to wield the rest. I did not expect the remaining 4 
eggs to all break at once! My caveman cannot possibly be that 
dextrous!


The rest of the game was not what I expected:

The high priest of Moloch was WAY rougher than I had expected. Next 
time around Im one shotting him with a stoning solution.

With Rodney I was anticipating some epic battle on every other dungeon 
level with him summoning crazy amounts of stuff, stealing my 
artifact/amulet, and using finger of death on me. Every single time he 
showed up I just zapped him with a wand of death. His curses always 
cursed my wands and his summons basically ignored me while I jumped 
off with jumping boots.

The planes were tedious for the most part. I blindfolded myself to 
avoid seeing copious amounts of log spam. Water was pretty relaxing. I 
just floated around until I got hungry and saw a piece of food. When I 
walked over to get it, apparently the portal was right on top. Since I 
had not #Invoke'd my sceptre to turn off conflict I got 4 angry 
angels. It took me three tries to find the correct altar (is there any 
easier way of determining altar type? I had to walk over the altar, 
drop a piece of food, walk off, and walk back on the altar! Four 
moves!?) Both Pestilence and Death ended up in melee range at some 
point. Famine never got close, which figured since I was encumbered on 
the planes from carrying 30 K-rations.

Overall I had a lot of fun. This character was fairly lucky and I 
played really safely. It took me a long time and lots of silly 
mistakes to ascend, but I'm just happy that I finally beat this game. 
I remember back when I played Nethack in elementary school thinking 
that no one could beat it without using backups of saved games, wizard 
mode, etc.




